# Code Owners - Require review from specific people/teams
# Learn more: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Global owners (fallback for all files)
* @your-github-username

# Backend code requires backend team review
/webapp/backend/ @your-org/backend-team @your-github-username
/chatbot/ @your-org/backend-team @your-github-username

# Frontend code requires frontend team review
/webapp/frontend/ @your-org/frontend-team @your-github-username
/frontend/ @your-org/frontend-team @your-github-username

# Database migrations require extra scrutiny
/database/ @your-org/backend-team @your-org/admins
/database/migrations/ @your-org/backend-team @your-org/admins

# Infrastructure & CI/CD require admin approval
/.github/ @your-org/admins @your-github-username
/k8s/ @your-org/admins @your-org/devops-team
/docker/ @your-org/admins @your-org/devops-team
/scripts/ @your-org/admins @your-org/devops-team

# Security-sensitive files require admin approval
.env.example @your-org/admins
/.gitignore @your-org/admins
/CODEOWNERS @your-org/admins

# Documentation can be reviewed by anyone
/docs/ @your-org/maintainers
README.md @your-org/maintainers
